# Intent: The brain step of the first run offers two equal routes (owner decision 34, 2026-11-18): A "Hosted by M5Stack/Xiaozhi" and B "Custom", each with one plain line about where the voice goes (A: to their servers, outside the home; B: where you point it), in all six languages. B opens the page with the three ways (MaiPai Home, my own servers, set one up for me). Neither route is highlighted and neither is an extra. A saves mode 3 (MFR_MODE_HOSTED) and sends it in first_run_done like the other modes; Skip still takes the old default (Home or set one up), never A. Back from the Custom page returns to the two routes.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_firstrun_core.h, maipai_firstrun.cc (ours, patches UX12 and UX13d)
# Check after a flash: first run step 4 shows two tiles with one line each and no tile highlighted; tapping Custom shows the three ways with a Back arrow that returns to the two tiles; tapping Hosted goes on to the privacy step and first_run_done carries mode 3; Skip still lands on Home or set one up.
# Kconfig: none

